# The explanation of each property row, the tooltip of its label: `field-help-<kind>-<path>`, else the
# member's `field-help-word-<member>` (see `strings::field_help`).
field-help-word-id = The record's unique ID. It never changes, so links to the record keep working.
field-help-word-source-ref = Where the record came from when it was imported. An import uses it to find the record again; read only.
field-help-word-key = The record's key in the file it was imported from.
field-help-word-lineage = The import that brought the record into the project.
field-help-word-page = The page this is drawn on. Move it on the page or cut and paste it to change that.
field-help-word-colour = The wire colour as an IEC 60757 code (BK, BU, GNYE). A colour set here comes before the colour profile and the defaults.
field-help-word-csa = The cross-section of the wire in mm². A value set here comes before the size profile and the defaults.
field-help-word-insulation = The insulation type of the wire. A value set here comes before the project's default.
field-help-word-wire-part = The wire part from the library that the wire is made of; the wire list and the bill of materials name it.
field-help-word-function = The wire's function word, which the wire list prints. A value set here comes before the project's default.
field-help-word-shielded = Whether the wire is shielded. Ticked here, it is shielded whatever the levels below say.
field-help-word-twisted = Whether the wire is twisted in a pair. Ticked here, it is twisted whatever the levels below say.
field-help-word-flags = Whether the wire is shielded or twisted.
field-help-word-potential = The potential the wire or point lies on: the name its definition gives, else a name from the connections. Define potential… sets its name, type and voltage.
field-help-connection-kind = What kind of connection this is: a wire, a bridge or a tube.
field-help-connection-line-kind = What the tube carries: working, pilot, exhaust or drain, or a flexible hose. It sets how the tube is drawn.
field-help-connection-tube-part = The tube part of this tube, over the one its medium or the project gives; empty takes that one again.
field-help-connection-tube-length = The length of this tube in millimetres, or typed with its unit (2 m, 35 cm); empty: the length is missing.
field-help-connection-derived-from-end = What the fitter puts on the wire's From end: by the rule table (not yet confirmed by a panel builder), or as set by hand. Set it here or in the Connections table; Reset gives the rule's back.
field-help-connection-derived-from-marker = What the marker on the wire's From end says, by the project's marking (the far end by default) or as set by hand; — for no marker. Reset gives the marking's back.
field-help-connection-derived-from-part = The ferrule or ring lug part of the From end: the first of the workshop stock that fits, or one set by hand.
field-help-connection-derived-medium = The medium the tube's net carries and where it is defined. Choosing one defines it at the tube's end, for every tube it reaches.
field-help-connection-derived-bus-cable = The bus cable that carries this line, listed in the cable overview and the parts list. Change it with Cable….
field-help-connection-derived-bus-plugs = The plug at each end of this line, by the port it sits on, listed in the parts list. Change them with Cable….
field-help-connection-derived-to-end = What the fitter puts on the wire's To end: by the rule table (not yet confirmed by a panel builder), or as set by hand. Set it here or in the Connections table; Reset gives the rule's back.
field-help-connection-derived-to-marker = What the marker on the wire's To end says, by the project's marking (the far end by default) or as set by hand; — for no marker. Reset gives the marking's back.
field-help-connection-derived-to-part = The ferrule or ring lug part of the To end: the first of the workshop stock that fits, or one set by hand.
field-help-connection-derived-tube = What the tube is: its size and material, from the project's default tube, its medium's, its tube part or its own. The chip names the source.
field-help-connection-number = The wire number as typed or frozen. Leave it empty to let wire numbering give it.
field-help-connection-derived-number = The wire number that is printed: from wire numbering, unless it is frozen. Freeze keeps it when the numbering changes.
field-help-connection-derived-colour = The colour the wire gets: its own override, else its cable core, its potential's definition, the colour profile or a default. The chip names the source; Go to source shows it.
field-help-connection-derived-csa = The cross-section the wire gets: its own override, else its cable core, its potential's definition, the size profile or a default. The chip names the source; Go to source shows it.
field-help-connection-derived-length = The length the fitter cuts the wire to, typed by hand, in millimetres or with its unit (2 m); a cable core is cut with its cable. The wire list prints it; a wire without one prints —.
field-help-connection-derived-way = Where Route laid the wire in its cabinet: the ducts it runs along, "door" where it crosses into a door, "direct" over the fronts. Route on the cabinet's panel page lays it again.
field-help-connection-derived-insulation = The insulation type the wire gets: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-wire-part = The wire part the wire gets: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-function = The function word the wire gets: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-shielded = Whether the wire is shielded: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-twisted = Whether the wire is twisted: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-overrides = The values set on this wire alone. Each comes before every other source of that value.
field-help-connection-overrides-colour = A colour for this wire alone. Clear it to give the wire the colour of its potential or profile again.
field-help-connection-overrides-csa = A cross-section for this wire alone. Clear it to give the wire that of its potential or profile again.
field-help-connection-overrides-end-a = The wire's end at this connection's end A, set by hand: what the fitter puts on it and its part. Reset gives the rule's back.
field-help-connection-overrides-end-a-part = The ferrule or ring lug part, one the project holds. Empty: the first of the workshop stock that fits.
field-help-connection-overrides-end-a-treatment = What the fitter puts on the end: a ferrule, a twin ferrule, a ring lug or nothing. Empty: the rule's.
field-help-connection-overrides-end-b = The wire's end at this connection's end B, set by hand: what the fitter puts on it and its part. Reset gives the rule's back.
field-help-connection-overrides-end-b-part = The ferrule or ring lug part, one the project holds. Empty: the first of the workshop stock that fits.
field-help-connection-overrides-end-b-treatment = What the fitter puts on the end: a ferrule, a twin ferrule, a ring lug or nothing. Empty: the rule's.
field-help-connection-overrides-length = A length for this wire, typed by hand, for the wire list. Clear it when the length is not known.
field-help-connection-overrides-show-marker = Whether the wire prints its annotation on the page: its number, cross-section and colour beside the wire.
field-help-connection-a = Where the wire starts: a connection point of a device or a junction.
field-help-connection-b = Where the wire ends: a connection point of a device or a junction.
field-help-connection-computed = Whether the program found this wire's route (the Wire tool between two clicks, or Route): Route may draw it again; a route you shape by hand is yours and Route leaves it alone.
field-help-word-route = The corners of the wire's path on the page, as grid cells. Drag the selected wire's handles on the page to change them.
field-help-potential-def-name = The potential's name (L1, 24VDC). Wires and points on the potential are known by it.
field-help-potential-def-ptype = The kind of signal the potential carries: a phase, neutral, PE, DC plus or minus, or a signal. The colour profile chooses the wire colour by it.
field-help-potential-def-voltage = The potential's voltage in volts. The colour and size profiles choose by it, and the checks read it.
field-help-potential-def-env = Whether the potential is AC or DC, its frequency and its earthing.
field-help-potential-def-env-ac-dc = Whether the potential is alternating (AC) or direct (DC) current.
field-help-potential-def-env-frequency = The frequency of an AC potential in hertz.
field-help-potential-def-env-earthing = How an extra-low voltage is earthed: PELV, SELV or floating.
field-help-potential-def-circuit-class = The circuit class of the potential: mains, control, analogue, bus or PE. The size profile chooses the cross-section by it; empty, it is derived.
field-help-potential-def-props = Wire properties for every wire on the potential. They come before the profiles and the defaults; a wire's own override comes before them.
field-help-potential-def-at = The point where the potential is defined: a connection point or a junction.
field-help-device-derived-tag = The device's tag as printed (-101K1). Derived: the numbering makes it from the device's page, letter and counter, and changes it when the device moves. Freeze keeps it as it is now, whatever the numbering does; typing another tag here freezes that one.
field-help-device-derived-valve-positions = What each valve position of the valve terminal holds: a valve, a blanking plate, or nothing. A position is filled where it is drawn, or in the station's rack (Rack…).
field-help-device-tag = How the device's tag is made: its letter, its counter, a frozen tag and the numbering scheme.
field-help-device-tag-letter = The code letter of the tag (K for a contactor). Changing it renumbers the device.
field-help-device-tag-counter = The number in the device's tag, such as 1 in -101K1. Numbering keeps it; empty, it gives the next free number. Another number here retags the device and its cross-references follow.
field-help-device-tag-frozen = A tag kept as typed: numbering no longer changes it. Unfreeze to let numbering give the tag again.
field-help-device-tag-frozen-sign = Whether pages print the minus sign before the frozen tag.
field-help-device-tag-frozen-text = The tag the device prints while it is frozen, such as S51: numbering never changes it. Its minus sign is the Sign row's.
field-help-device-tag-scheme = The numbering scheme of this device; empty, the project's.
field-help-device-function-text = What the device does, in words (Main switch). The lists print it; on the page it prints beside the tag where the symbol has a place for it, else over the device's path with Function text over its path (this row's … menu or the symbol's right-click menu, a symbol selected).
field-help-device-kind = What sort of device this is. It guides the tag letter and numbering.
field-help-device-state = Where the device is in its life: in use, a spare or planned.
field-help-device-parent = The device this one belongs to (an assembly, a manifold). Its tag follows the parent's.
field-help-device-position = The device's place inside its parent, such as a valve's place on a manifold.
field-help-device-process-tag = The process tag from the process drawing. Numbering never changes it.
field-help-device-parts = The parts the device is built from, each with its quantity. Choose part… adds one from the library.
field-help-device-parts-item-part = The part from the library, by its number and manufacturer.
field-help-device-parts-item-qty = How many of the part the device uses, such as 2 for two auxiliary contact blocks: the parts list counts the part that many times for the device.
field-help-device-tech-data = Technical data of the device, each a name and a value (rated current, coil voltage).
field-help-device-tech-data-item-key = The name of one technical value, such as rated_current or characteristic. The device's tech data text prints its values in name order, and a value of the device comes before the part's value of the same name.
field-help-device-tech-data-item-value = The value itself: a number with its unit, such as 40 A or 24 V, or a word, such as C. A characteristic and a rated current in amperes print together as C10.
field-help-device-derived-cp-item = A connection point of the device, as pages print it. Mark not used tells the checks it stays free on purpose.
field-help-device-derived-main-location = Where the device's main symbol stands: its page and grid cell.
field-help-device-derived-position = The valve's place on its valve terminal. Type another free position to move it there; a valve placed inside the valve terminal's box takes the next free one.
field-help-device-derived-medium = The medium this source supplies and where it is defined. Choose one to define it at the source's port, for every tube it reaches; New medium… makes one first.
field-help-device-derived-printed-label = The text the device prints beside its tag.
field-help-device-derived-group = The group of the terminal on its strip. Typing a caption here names the group.
field-help-device-derived-structure-function = The function (=) identifier the tag uses: set on the device, else taken from its page or a structure box.
field-help-device-derived-structure-location = The location (+) identifier the tag uses: set on the device, else taken from its page or a structure box.
field-help-word-structure = The structure identifiers set here. One left empty is taken from the page or a structure box.
field-help-device-structure-function = The function (=) identifier of the device. Empty, the page's or a structure box's applies.
field-help-page-structure-function = The function (=) identifier of the page; the devices on it take it unless they set their own.
field-help-word-location = The location (+) identifier: where it is mounted. Devices without their own take the page's.
field-help-word-document-kind = The document kind (&) identifier of the structure.
field-help-word-functional-assignment = The functional assignment (==) identifier of the structure.
field-help-word-installation-site = The installation site (++) identifier: the plant or building.
field-help-word-type = The type (#) identifier of the structure.
field-help-word-user-defined = An identifier of your own kind, beside the standard ones.
field-help-device-strip = The terminal strip's own settings: how its terminals are named and printed.
field-help-device-strip-accessories = The strip's accessories (end brackets, covers) in mounting order.
field-help-device-strip-designation-scheme = How the terminals are numbered: 1, 2, 3 or another scheme.
field-help-device-strip-field-side = Which side of the terminals faces the field wiring.
field-help-word-groups = Groups of terminals on the strip, each with a caption.
field-help-device-strip-groups-item-from-seq = The first terminal of the group, by its place on the strip.
field-help-device-strip-groups-item-to-seq = The last terminal of the group, by its place on the strip.
field-help-device-strip-groups-item-label = The group's caption, printed above its terminals.
field-help-device-strip-label-mode = What each terminal of the strip prints at its symbol: its designation (1, 2, PE), or its function text (1+) where it has one.
field-help-device-strip-tag-print = Where the strip's tag is printed: once per segment or at every terminal.
field-help-device-terminal = This terminal's settings on its strip.
field-help-device-terminal-designation = The terminal's designation (1, 2, PE), printed at the terminal.
field-help-device-terminal-levels = The levels of a multi-level terminal, each with its own connection points.
field-help-device-terminal-rail-bonded = Whether the terminal is bonded to the mounting rail, as a PE terminal is.
field-help-device-terminal-seq = The terminal's place on its strip, for drawing and mounting; its designation may differ.
field-help-device-terminal-strip = The strip this terminal belongs to.
field-help-device-cable = The cable's own settings: its length and how its cores are named.
field-help-device-cable-core-id-mode = How the cable's cores are identified: by number or by colour.
field-help-device-cable-length = Where the cable's length comes from, or the length itself.
field-help-device-cable-pre-assembled = Whether the cable comes pre-assembled with its connectors.
field-help-device-plc-module = The PLC module's settings: its slot and its first addresses. A module gets them from its station, so it has none until it sits in a station's rack (the PLC panel lists a module under its station).
field-help-device-plc-module-integrated = Whether the module is built into the station's CPU.
field-help-device-plc-module-part-use = Which of the device's parts is the module.
field-help-device-plc-module-slot = The module's slot in the rack: auto for the next free one, or a number.
field-help-device-plc-module-start = The first input and output addresses of the module.
field-help-device-plc-module-start-input = The module's first input address: auto, or an address such as I4.0.
field-help-device-plc-module-start-output = The module's first output address: auto, or an address such as Q4.0.
field-help-device-plc-module-safety = The safety data of an F-module: its F-destination and F-source addresses, its watchdog time and the address range of its device description.
field-help-device-plc-station = The PLC station's settings: its configuration project and its order.
field-help-device-plc-station-config-project = The PLC configuration project the station belongs to.
field-help-device-plc-station-order = The station's place among the stations of its configuration project.
field-help-device-plc-station-role = The station's role, such as the head station or a remote one.
field-help-device-assembly = The assembly's settings: what its bill of materials lists.
field-help-device-assembly-bom-basis = Whether the bill of materials lists the assembly's order codes or its components.
field-help-word-configs = The assembly's order codes, order code 1 first. In the assembly's bill of materials each order code with a part prints one line in place of the part lines of the devices it covers.
field-help-word-covers = The devices whose own part lines this order code replaces in the bill of materials.
field-help-device-assembly-configs-item-label = A name of your own for the order code, such as Order code 1, to tell several apart here; nothing prints it.
field-help-word-order-code = The order code as the supplier writes it, such as 8WD4420-5AB; a symbol's order-code text prints the first one.
field-help-device-assembly-configs-item-part = The configured part of the order code: the assembly's bill of materials prints it as one line, and a symbol prints its manufacturer beside the order code.
field-help-function-kind = What the function is: a normal function, an interruption point or a black box.
field-help-function-kind-ip = The interruption point's settings: its name, direction and order.
field-help-function-kind-ip-name = The name that pairs this interruption point with the others of the same name; the cross-reference shows where they are.
field-help-function-kind-ip-direction = Whether the signal leaves (source) or arrives (target) here, or goes both ways.
field-help-function-kind-ip-sort = The point's place in the chain of points with the same name.
field-help-function-kind-ip-star-source = Whether this point is the one the others of its name start from, in star mode.
field-help-function-kind-ip-external = The point outside the project this interruption point leads to.
field-help-function-role = Whether the function is the device's main function or an auxiliary one (a contact of a contactor).
field-help-function-def = The function definition this function was made from: its connection points and their names.
field-help-function-device = The device the function belongs to.
field-help-function-template-entry = Which function of the part this is, with its connection point names.
field-help-word-cp-overrides = Changes to single connection points of this function: another name, a description, or not used.
field-help-word-idx = Which connection point of the function this is, by its number in the function.
field-help-word-alias = A second name of the connection point, printed with its own (1 / L1).
field-help-function-cp-overrides-item-designation = The name the connection point prints instead of its definition's.
field-help-function-cp-overrides-item-description = Words of your own about the connection point, such as Supply 24 V. The project keeps them with the point; no page or list prints them yet.
field-help-function-cp-overrides-item-closure-kind = How the fluid port is closed: with a plug, with a silencer, or blanked.
field-help-function-cp-overrides-item-closure-part = The part of the plug or the silencer that closes the fluid port.
field-help-word-unused = Whether the connection point stays free on purpose; its unconnected-point finding is then only an info.
field-help-word-closure = How an unused fluid port is closed: a plug, a silencer or a blanking.
field-help-word-bus-port = The function's port on a field bus: its bus, address and net.
field-help-function-bus-port-address = The station address on the bus, or TBD while it is not known.
field-help-word-bus = The field bus the port is on, such as PROFINET or PROFIBUS DP; the bus lists and the bus checks take the port by it.
field-help-word-interface = The name of the device's interface the port belongs to, as its part names it, such as X1 or DP; the PLC exchange matches the port by it.
field-help-word-logical-net = The logical net of the port: where its address must be unique.
field-help-word-physical-net = The physical net whose cable segments the port belongs to.
field-help-word-port-label = The port's label on an interface with several ports (P1R).
field-help-function-bus-port-role = The port's role on its bus: a master or controller that addresses the others, a slave or device with an address of its own, or a passive connector without one.
field-help-function-bus-port-mrp = The port's role in a PROFINET ring (MRP): manager or client; empty without a ring.
field-help-word-termination = Whether the bus terminating resistor at this port is switched on. On a PROFIBUS segment the terminating element at each end must be on and every other one off (EW-BUS-004); the bus list prints it.
field-help-representation-derived-xref = The cross-reference the symbol prints: where its other symbols or paired points are, by the project's format.
field-help-representation-pos = Where the symbol stands on the page, in millimetres and its grid cell. Move it on the page to change it.
field-help-representation-orient = How the symbol is turned and mirrored. Rotate and Mirror change it.
field-help-representation-symbol = The symbol from the library that draws this function.
field-help-representation-variant = The symbol's variant, such as another contact image.
field-help-representation-rep-type = Which view the symbol belongs to: multi-line, single-line or another.
field-help-word-functions = The functions this symbol draws.
field-help-representation-anchor = The point of the symbol whose grid cell names it, such as 103-C4 in its cross-references and its device's place: its origin, the place of one of its texts, the centre of its drawing or a point of its own. Empty, the symbol's own choice.
field-help-representation-arrangement = Which of the symbol's texts it shows, by a set its symbol names, such as full (tag, data, cross-reference and pin names) or tag (the tag alone). Empty, each text as the symbol has it; a text shown or hidden here wins over both.
field-help-representation-pin-map = Which connection point of the symbol stands for which of the function.
field-help-representation-box = The outline and connection points of a black box.
field-help-word-cps = The connection points of the black box, each with its place and direction.
field-help-representation-box-cps-item-pos = Where the connection point lies on the box.
field-help-representation-box-cps-item-name = The pin's name on a box drawn without a part; a box of a part prints its part's pin names.
field-help-word-dir = The direction a wire leaves the connection point.
field-help-word-outline = The corners of the black box's outline.
field-help-representation-box-inner = Whether the box is drawn inside another symbol.
field-help-representation-box-slots = A valve terminal's box drawn as its valve positions: one cell per position in a row; absent, a free box.
field-help-representation-box-slots-pitch = The width of one cell, set from the page grid.
field-help-word-text-slots = The symbol's texts that are moved, turned or hidden here, each by its slot.
field-help-representation-text-slots-item-slot = Which text of the symbol this changes, by its slot: the tag, the function text, the technical data, a pin's name.
field-help-representation-text-slots-item-pos = Where the text stands, in millimetres from the symbol's origin as the unturned symbol has it, such as x -3.3, y 2.6; empty, where the symbol puts it. Dragging the text sets it.
field-help-word-angle = The angle the text prints at, in degrees counter-clockwise, such as 90 to read from the bottom; empty, the symbol's own. Turning the symbol never turns its texts.
field-help-word-visible = Shows or hides this one text on this symbol, whatever its arrangement says.
field-help-junction-at = Where the junction stands on the page, in millimetres from the page's top left corner, on its grid; the wires joined there end at it.
field-help-word-sequence = The wires of the junction in wiring order; the first is the feed.
field-help-junction-style = How the junction is drawn: a dot, or a bevel, a short slant that shows which way the wires branch. The Wire tool joins with a bevel.
field-help-junction-wiring = Whether the wires are joined as a star or a chain; empty, the style's default.
field-help-page-item-kind = What the item is: a text, a graphic, an image, a wire annotation, a view of a mounting surface or an underlay.
field-help-page-item-kind-underlay = A PDF page or DXF drawing placed under the page to redraw over. It is locked, and no check, report or export reads it.
field-help-page-item-kind-free-text = A text of your own on the page, as you write it or bound to a project or page property whose value it prints. The layout never moves it.
field-help-page-item-kind-graphic = A line, polyline, rectangle, circle, arc or polygon of your own, with its pen and fill. It prints as it is drawn; no check or report reads it.
field-help-page-item-kind-image = A picture in a rectangle of the page, in millimetres: the project keeps its file and prints it at that size.
field-help-page-item-kind-wire-marker = A marker across several wires that names them together: their numbers, or the cable they run in, printed at its line.
field-help-page-item-kind-surface-view = The view of one mounting surface on a panel layout page: which surface it draws, what its devices print and the point its positions are measured from.
field-help-word-surface = The mounting surface the page shows.
field-help-word-label-mode = What the placed devices print on the layout: their tag, part or nothing.
field-help-word-datum = The surface's point from which positions are measured.
field-help-word-datum-at = Where the measuring point of the surface lies on the page.
field-help-page-item-layer = A layer name of your own for the item, such as Notes. This version keeps it, and draws, prints and exports every item whatever its layer.
field-help-page-title = The page's title, printed in its title block and in the table of contents.
field-help-page-folio = The page's folio: its number and section.
field-help-page-folio-number = The page's number, such as 101: the pages stand in its order within their section, and the title block, the table of contents and Prev and Next print it unless the page has a label of its own.
field-help-page-folio-section = The section the page belongs to.
field-help-page-folio-label = A folio label of your own, such as 101a.
field-help-page-kind = The page type: schematic, panel layout, report or another.
field-help-page-derived-description = The description the title block prints: the project's description, unless the page overrides it.
field-help-page-description-override = A description for this page alone, instead of the project's.
field-help-page-form = A frame of its own for this page, instead of the project's.
field-help-page-scale = The scale the page is drawn at, such as 1:10, or not to scale. The title block prints it after the page's title; a panel layout page draws its plate at it, and a new layout takes the scale its plate fits the sheet at.
field-help-page-grid = The page's connection grid: the step that symbols, pins and wires snap to, such as 4 mm, or 10 px for a page brought in from QElectroTech. Page ▸ Connection grid… changes it and fits what the page holds.
field-help-page-grid-num = The grid step in nanometres before the divisor: 4 000 000 over 1 is the 4 mm grid, 7 937 500 over 3 the 10 px grid of QElectroTech.
field-help-page-grid-den = The divisor of the grid step, 1 for a step of whole nanometres, such as 3 for the 10 px grid of QElectroTech (7 937 500 over 3).
field-help-section-title = The section's title, such as Wiring definition: its divider page prints it, and the table of contents lists it.
field-help-section-number = The section's number, such as 1: the sections stand in its order, and its divider page prints it (Section 1).
field-help-section-divider = Whether the program makes a divider page at the section's first folio, with the section's number, folios and title.
field-help-section-folio-range = The first and last folio of the section's pages, such as 100 to 199: a page whose number lies in it belongs to the section, and its divider page takes the first.
field-help-report-block-derived-kind = The page type of a generated page: report.
field-help-report-block-title = The title of the report's pages, which their title blocks and the table of contents print, such as Parts list {n}: {n} is the page's number in the report, {count} its number of pages, {group} the group the page lists, {layout} the folio of the layout page a legend follows.
field-help-report-block-source = What the report lists: devices, wires, terminals or parts.
field-help-report-block-form = The form the report's first page is laid out on, by its name: its frame, its title block and the table's columns and rows; that form names the form of the further pages.
field-help-report-block-continuation = How the report's further pages are numbered: after the first folio as 907.1, 907.2 (the default), or with the next folios, 908, 909.
field-help-report-block-section = The section the report's pages are numbered in; empty, they stand before the sections, with the front matter.
field-help-report-block-first-folio = The folio of the report's first page, such as 901; its further pages follow it as 901.1, 901.2 or take the next numbers, as its continuation says.
field-help-report-block-sort = The columns the report's rows are sorted by, each up or down, in natural order (K2 before K10); empty, the report's own order.
field-help-report-block-group = The column the report's rows are grouped by, and whether a new group goes on, starts a new page or a new folio.
field-help-report-block-empty = What the report prints when it lists nothing: no pages (the default), or one page with a text of your own.
field-help-report-block-embedded = Whether the report is printed inside another page.
field-help-report-block-manual = Rows added to or left out of the report by hand.
field-help-word-include = Records added to the report by hand.
field-help-word-exclude = Records left out of the report by hand.
field-help-project-kind = Whether this is a schematic project, a template or a macro project.
field-help-project-basic-project = The template this project was made from, recorded when it was made. The project holds its own copy of what the template gave it, so a later change to the template changes nothing here.
field-help-project-control-voltage = The project's nominal control voltage, typed with its unit, such as 24 V. The program keeps it as a note: no title block, list or check reads it yet; the colour and size profiles and the checks use each potential's own voltage, set at its definition.
field-help-project-derivation-profile = The version of the rules that derive tags, colours and sizes.
field-help-project-rated-consumption = The current the equipment draws at full load, typed with its unit, such as 16 A. The program keeps it as a note: no title block, list or check reads it yet.
field-help-project-languages = The project's languages: the one texts are written in, and the translations.
field-help-project-languages-source = The language the project's texts are written in; every other language is a translation of them.
field-help-project-languages-translations = The languages the project's texts are translated into, each kept beside the text it translates.
field-help-project-master = The project's own data, which the title blocks print.
field-help-project-master-description = The project's description; every page prints it unless it overrides it.
field-help-project-master-document-title = The title of the whole document set, such as Electrical documentation: the cover page prints it.
field-help-project-master-long-description = A longer description of the project, over several lines if need be: the cover page prints it under Project Description.
field-help-project-master-drawing-id = The drawing ID of the document set, such as EL-001: the title block prints it in its Drawing cell on every page, and the cover page under Drawing Identification.
field-help-project-master-object-id = The ID of the object or machine the project is for, such as Line 3: the title block prints it in its Object cell, and the cover page prints it too.
field-help-project-master-project-ref = The project reference, such as the order number of the job: the title block prints it in its Project cell, and the cover page under Project Reference.
field-help-project-master-manufacturing-year = The year the equipment is built, such as 2026. The program keeps it with the project: no title block or list prints it yet.
field-help-project-master-created = The date the project was made, such as 14-03-2026: the title block prints it in its Creation cell and the cover page under Created On, in the project's date format.
field-help-project-master-edited = The date of the last save that held a change, which every such save sets itself: the title block prints it in its Saved cell and the cover page under Edited On. It cannot be typed.
field-help-word-parties = The people and companies of the project: customer, end user, panel builder, author.
field-help-project-parties-item-name = The party's name, such as the end user's company: a title block or the cover page prints the name of the first party of a role in that role's cell, such as End user.
field-help-project-parties-item-role = The party's role in the project: customer, end user, panel builder, author, checker or engineer. A title block's cell of a role prints the first party that has it.
field-help-project-parties-item-address = The party's street, postcode, city and country: the cover page prints the end user's in its Address, Postcode / City and Country lines.
field-help-word-street = The street and number of the party's address, such as Main Street 12: a title block or cover page with a cell for it prints it.
field-help-word-postcode = The postcode of the party's address, such as 1234 AB: a title block or cover page with a cell for it prints it.
field-help-word-city = The city of the party's address: a title block or cover page with a cell for it prints it.
field-help-word-country = The country of the party's address: a title block or cover page with a cell for it prints it.
field-help-project-parties-item-personal-data = Whether the party is a person whose data must be protected.
field-help-project-settings = The project's settings: numbering, profiles, formats and checks.
field-help-project-settings-frames = The frame every drawn page prints on while it names none of its own: the project's default, and one for each page type that has its own; a section divider takes its type's. The lists, the generated table of contents among them, print on Frame of the lists in Main and never on these: the Table of contents entry frames a contents page drawn by hand.
field-help-project-settings-colour-profile = The colour profile: which wire colour each kind of potential gets. Change it in the wizard.
field-help-project-settings-size-profile = The size profile: which cross-section each circuit class gets. Change it in the wizard.
field-help-project-settings-numbering = How device tags and wire numbers are made.
field-help-project-settings-xref-format = How cross-references are written, such as 102-A1.
field-help-project-settings-text-styles = The project's text styles: fonts and sizes.
field-help-project-settings-typeface = The font file of the project's own that every text in the Standard typeface prints in. Choose it in Text styles.
field-help-project-settings-workshop = The project's settings for the workshop: the stock the shop keeps and what the cut list cuts to.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-device-labels = Where a device's label goes: on the device, or on the device and beside it on the mounting plate (two labels); empty: on the device.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-mark-cores = Whether a cable's cores carry a marker at each end; empty: no, a core's colour or number and its cable's marker name it.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-mark-jumpers = Whether a jumper between two pins of one device carries a marker; empty: no.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-marking = What the marker on each wire end says: the far end, the wire's number, both ends on two lines, or the potential; empty: the far end.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-stock = The wires, ferrules and markers the shop keeps, in its order of preference: a wire, a wire end and a label take the first that fits them.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-stock-item = One part the shop keeps.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-cut-increment = What the cut list rounds each piece up to; empty: 5 mm.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-ferrules = Which fine-stranded wire ends take a ferrule: every one, or every one but those into a spring or push-in clamp, which holds the strands itself; empty: every one but those into a spring or push-in clamp.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-label-profile = The label file the label program imports: its columns with the headings it prints, its form and a CSV's delimiter; empty: an Excel file with the generic columns Text 1, Text 2, Text 3, Copies and For.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-label-profile-delimiter = What separates the columns of a label file's CSV: a comma or a semicolon; empty: a comma.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-label-profile-file = The form of a label file: an Excel file or a CSV; empty: Excel.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-two-wires = What two wires of one size on one clamp take: one twin ferrule, where the clamp takes one, or a ferrule each; empty: a twin ferrule.
field-help-project-settings-workshop-reserve = What the fitter adds to a routed wire at each end: stripping, the bend into the clamp and a little to spare; empty: 50 mm (a fixed reserve of 50 to 150 mm per wire is usual; not verified).
field-help-project-settings-workshop-fill-limit = How full, in percent of its inner area, Route lets a duct be where it is fullest before it lays a wire another way; EW-LAY-008 reports a duct over it; empty: 60 % (not verified).
field-help-project-settings-workshop-door-loop = The loop a wire into a door keeps across the hinge, added to its routed length; empty: 300 mm (not verified).
