field-committed-route-ends-item-h = Height
field-committed-route-run = Run
field-committed-route-way = Way
field-committed-route-way-item = Step
field-project-lists-form = Frame of the lists
field-help-project-lists-form = The frame every list prints on (the parts list, the terminal and cable lists, the contents): a frame chosen here goes to every list at once, each list keeping it as its report block's Form. On a set of another paper size, a list prints on the set's own frame.
field-help-project-settings-drawing-wire-numbers = Whether every wire prints its number on the pages, in the PDF and in print: one setting for the whole project. Number wires by potential (Draw ▸ Connect) decides what the numbers are.
field-help-project-supply = The supply the equipment is connected to: its voltage, phases, conductors and earthing. The cover page prints it as one line, such as 3 x 400 VAC + N + PE, 50 Hz.
field-help-project-supply-u-nom = The supply's nominal voltage in volts, such as 400 for a 400 V three-phase supply: the cover page's Supply line prints it, and Potential… on a supply mark named L1, L2 or L3 offers it as the mark's voltage.
field-help-project-supply-frequency = The supply's frequency in hertz, such as 50; 0 is a DC supply. The cover page's Supply line prints it (50 Hz), and VDC instead of VAC for 0.
field-help-project-supply-phases = The number of phases of the supply, such as 3 or 1: the cover page's Supply line starts with it (3 x 400 VAC).
field-help-project-supply-neutral = Whether the supply brings a neutral conductor: the cover page's Supply line then adds + N, such as 3 x 400 VAC + N.
field-help-project-supply-pe = Whether the supply brings a protective earth conductor: the cover page's Supply line then adds + PE, such as 3 x 400 VAC + N + PE.
field-help-project-supply-earthing = The supply's earthing system: TN-S, TN-C-S, TT or IT. The program keeps it with the project: the cover page's Supply line leaves it out, and no check reads it yet.
field-help-project-supply-origin = Where the supply comes from and how strong it is.
field-help-project-supply-origin-source = The point outside the project that feeds the equipment, such as the building's distribution board: an external reference with its location and device. The program keeps it with the project; no page prints it yet.
field-help-project-supply-origin-ik-max = The highest prospective short-circuit current at the supply point, in kA, such as 10. The program keeps it with the project: no check reads it yet.
field-help-project-supply-origin-upstream-rating = The rated current of the protection before the supply point, in A, such as 63. The program keeps it with the project: no check reads it yet.
field-help-device-parts-item = One part the device uses, with its quantity.
field-help-device-accessory-choices = The device's choices of the accessories its parts bring with them: one left off, or taken as another part.
field-help-device-accessory-choices-item = One accessory a part of the device brings with it, left off or taken as another part.
field-help-device-accessory-choices-item-of = The accessory the part brings with it that the choice is about.
field-help-device-accessory-choices-item-part = The part the accessory is taken as; empty: the device does without it.
field-help-device-tech-data-item = One technical value of the device: its name and value.
